  "fork_root_text": "[fork] replaces head through 81d50d467779ba683aab8f753075b06a79949c4c62e7e11018d724c6355229eb; forked_from eb46803990131cf6ca8c8ba7f6c4fcee5bc452e9561ac2307f33c96a071accf1\n\nHead summary (turns 1-20). Reproduced the p95 regression from fixtures/orders_2026_10.jsonl: cold 904 ms, warm 238 ms, so the cost is per-attempt, not per-request. Profiling puts about 61% of the delta inside retry_with_backoff; the wrapper re-validates the payload on every attempt and re-opens the Redis connection for each idempotency lookup. The retry budget is 500 ms with a 3-attempt cap; the 6 attempts seen in the fixture come from record_latency incrementing once per attempt, not from the budget. Decision: memoise the validated payload keyed by idempotency_key and cap attempts at 3; the response schema is unchanged. Open: whether ORDERS_FAST_PATH should default on in staging. Next: patch src/api/middleware/retry.py and rerun the replay.",
